<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">British Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as British</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The British Empire comprised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">dominions</a>, colonies, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorates</a> and other territories ruled or administered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> from the late sixteenth to the twentieth century. At its height it was the largest empire in history, covering about a quarter of the world's land. It conquered or absorbed many states covered by the site, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto</a> polities, and decolonised mainly after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/british-empire.jpg" alt="British Empire" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hoshie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Great_Britain_(1707%E2%80%931800).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
